---
description: TypeScript, React, and formatting conventions
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,css,json}"
alwaysApply: true
---

- Use strict TypeScript without `any`, explicit member accessibility, full variable names without abbreviations, and no unnecessary dependencies.
- Use four spaces and braces for all control-flow bodies.
- Format changed files with the configured formatter. Put nested JSX and JSX with more than five props on multiple lines.
- Write self-explanatory code. Do not add `// ponytail:` markers, AI annotations, or comments narrating shortcuts. Comments describe behavior; record genuine trade-offs in the commit message.
- Extract a block when a meaningful name such as `canDeleteProject`, `TimelineTicks`, or `useDragSelection` makes the codebase's language clearer. Do not extract code only to shorten a file.
- Keep top-level code focused on feature intent rather than implementation details.
- React Compiler handles routine memoization. Add `useMemo` or `useCallback` only when reference identity changes behavior, such as an identity-based registry or documented stable callback contract. Stable JSX props and paired effect setup/cleanup are not sufficient reasons. Define effect-only functions inside the effect.
